 scalpers"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Before seeking medical care outside your home province, ask locally first — the need for such care should ideally be assessed by an associate chief physician or higher"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/24-05","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Stop treating tertiary hospitals as mere prescription hubs — stable chronic disease patients should turn to primary care"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"If you have doubts about treatment, request to seal the medical records on the spot; both parties must be present, a list must be drawn up, and each side gets a copy"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After every medical visit, keep a personal copy of your medical records, test reports, and imaging scans"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Even without money or ID, and unable to identify yourself, emergency care must be provided first"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Disability assessments must be conducted only after treatment is complete; doing it too early results in a lower rating"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"After treatment, functional impairments may indeed remain; apply for a disability certificate at the county-level disability association in your hukou area"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Thank the doctors who saved you — send thank-you letters, banners, or satisfaction ratings instead of cash gifts. The rules prohibit money, not gratitude"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Before getting a dental implant, ask what the package price includes; prioritize providers committed to price regulation, and do not trust low-price ads"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/24"},"children":["Chapter 24"," ·"," ","Seeking medical care: How to save money and avoid unnecessary hassle"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"24-05"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["05"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Stop treating tertiary hospitals as mere prescription hubs — stable chronic disease patients should turn to primary care"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Moving forward, tertiary hospitals will primarily handle emergency cases, critically ill patients, and complex medical conditions. Routine follow-ups for common illnesses and regular outpatient visits for patients with stable chronic diseases will gradually be phased out. The same expert physicians who previously saw patients in tertiary hospitals will now provide care at community clinics. Continuing to use large hospitals solely for medication refills will become increasingly difficult as appointment slots dwindle."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"chi